I walk slowly through the quiet gallery.
Many old paintings hang here.
They show landscapes from Berlin.
I stop in front of two pictures.
They hang right next to each other.
I compare them in my head.
This picture here is very bright and colourful.
That picture next to it is quite dark.
I like this picture much better than that picture.
I take the mobile phone out of my pocket.
I quickly take a photo of the artwork.
I send the photo to my colleague Jonas.
We often talk about art at work.
I immediately write him a short message.
"Hello Jonas, do you remember our conversation?"
"We talked about art a few weeks ago."
"What do you think of this picture?"
I smile and send the message.
Then I walk leisurely to the next room.
